Implementation plan: release-manifest verifier (`p2-verifier`, part of project #6902)

Planning ref: `git rev-parse HEAD` = `fcd85f4a7e683d290461f6a7712b10026856a0ad`, symbolic branch `orchestrator/project-6902`. This matches the issue's integration branch metadata, so there is no mismatch.

Scope-mode: Hold Scope
Reuse-audit: extends scripts/release_manifest.py
Scope-mode justification: The issue asks for one stdlib verifier script, its tests and the CI registration, with no workflow behaviour change. Hold Scope keeps it there. The verifier imports the format constants and path-safety helper from `scripts/release_manifest.py` (`SCHEMA_VERSION`, `RELEASE_MANIFEST_REPOSITORY`, `TAG_RE`, `PATH_SEGMENT_RE`, `KNOWN_SYMLINKS`, `ManifestError`, `_safe_rel`) and `validate_release_sha` from `scripts/workflow_wrapper_refs.py`, so the format is not defined a second time. A parity test ties its stdlib schema check to `ai-memory/schemas/release_manifest.v1.json`. Two small additions are needed for CI to pass, so I'm taking them in this PR rather than deferring:
- a `docs/INVENTORY.md` line: `tests/inventory_parity.py` runs in CI and fails when a new `scripts/*` file is missing from the inventory;
- a changelog fragment.

Nothing goes into `.github/workflows/*.yml` other than appending one test path in `ci.yml`. Under §6, correctness and safety (failing closed on every input) come before speed.

